<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Anglo may restructure gold interests - paper.</title>
<headline>Anglo may restructure gold interests - paper.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo American Corp of South Africa Ltd is considering restructurng its gold interests, which could result in one or more mergers of its existing gold mining companies, Business Day reported on Monday.  </p>
<p>The paper quoted Anglogold chief executive Bobby Godsell saying &quot;we are reviewing our structure&quot;.</p>
<p>A restructuring by Anglo would follow similar moves by other South african mining houses. Gencor Ltd last year merged the four contiguous Evander mines while Anglovaal Ltd created Avgold, which brought together three gold producers and its new mine development interests in Target.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
